From 3ad96cc4cb253fa07811c3d9245b8af52ef2ccc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikko Huttunen <mikko.applets@example.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 12:52:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Lens/telescope explorer: fix stale-preset bug, telescope
 label overlap, add back-to-course link
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Preset-group and slider-row visibility (Single lens / Two lenses /
  Telescope) is now driven entirely by a single #layout[data-mode]
  attribute + CSS rules, instead of a sequence of individual
  element.style.display assignments in JS. This removes the failure
  mode where one bad/late DOM lookup could halt setMode() partway
  through and leave a previous tab's preset buttons (e.g. the
  two-lens Case 1-3 buttons) visibly stuck on top of the Telescope
  tab. Each tab now unambiguously owns its own Cases section.
- Telescope figure: the objective/eyepiece labels, focal-point ticks
  and the afocal status banner were competing for the same cramped
  vertical band and spilling past the SVG viewBox, rendering as
  overlapping/clipped text. Reworked the vertical layout with a
  dedicated header band for a single merged status line
  ("AFOCAL — rays leave parallel (θ=..° → θ'=..°, M=..×)" /
  "NOT afocal (Δd=..)"), and shrank the lens symbols slightly so
  their labels have headroom.
- Added a '← FYS.240 Optics' back-to-course link at the top of the
  page, matching the convention used by the other applets.
- If this still looks stale after deploying, it's most likely the
  registered service worker (service-worker.js) serving a cached
  copy — a hard refresh / clearing site data resolves that.
